file or a sub‐directory.  The field is valid for files only,  and
specifies the file’s size in bytes.  The field describes the file
or  directory’s  modification time, specified as seconds from the
Unix epoch.  The timestamp is relative to the  current  timezone,
so can be used to convert it into human readable form.  Note that
the Toppy sets directory timestamps to a predefined value so they
are not particularly useful.  The field is not used at this time.
This  command is used to initiate reading a file from the Toppy’s
